  "body": "**What.** State Theorem A(M = 5) once the controls are fixed and lemmas 6a(5) and 6b1 are certified.\n\n**Why.** Digest, item 2c; [PROOF.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/PROOF.md) stage 2; [notes/PROOF_QUEUE.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/notes/PROOF_QUEUE.md) P3.\n\n**Acceptance (each can fail).**\n- The note says exactly what the code proves, apart from the theorem it serves, and names Braaksma's theorem and the start-value lemma as assumptions.\n- Status word: certified, with the trusted code named.\n- `check_numbers.py --selftest` passes, with a check for any new headline number.\n\n**Depends on.** Add the midpoint D2 criterion to certify_M2.py d2check (M = 5 review 1, 3); Add the step-halving remainder check to certify_M2_lohner.py selftest; Keep arb upper bounds for hw and nu in certify_M2.py start_data2; Fix the M = 5 review's wording issues 5-7 in A_M2.md; Run lemma 6a(5) on the M = 5 certificate's exported box; Run lemma 6b1 at M = 5: 18 rows and 366 discs; Review the lemma 6a and 6b1 disc certificate code independently\n\n**Files.** [proof/A_lemmas_M.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/proof/A_lemmas_M.md), [PROOF.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/PROOF.md), [README.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/README.md), [notes/PROOF_QUEUE.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/notes/PROOF_QUEUE.md)",
